$ ==========================================================================
$ ALIQ - Ca-CaO liquidus   (VERIFICATION, set weight 0 before optimizing)
$
$ HALITE#1 fixed at ZERO, which is how to say "the liquid is just
$ saturated". LIQUID entered and free, satisfying R1.
$ Conditions: P, T, N, X(SR) = 4, plus 1 fixed phase = 5.
$ ==========================================================================

$ No TABLE_HEAD, for the same reason as in AGAPT (R8): the starting CaO
$ fraction in the liquid has to follow the composition of each point. In
$ the previous table the 12 rows shared Y(LIQUID,CAO)=0.05 and only 6 of
$ the 12 equilibria compiled.
$ Starting y_CaO = x(O)/(1-x(O)), which is the exact relation of the
$ associate model when y_O is negligible.

$ 1280 K, x(O)=0.0250, DTA
CREATE_NEW_EQUILIBRIUM 21,1
CHANGE_STATUS PHASE LIQUID=ENTERED 1
CHANGE_STATUS PHASE HALITE#1=FIX 0
SET-CONDITION P=P0,T=1280,N=1,X(SR)=0
EXPERIMENT X(LIQUID,O)=0.0250:DXL
LABEL ALIQ
SET_START_VALUE Y(LIQUID,CA)=0.9744
SET_START_VALUE Y(LIQUID,CAO)=0.0256
SET_START_VALUE Y(HALITE#1,CA)=1

$ 1283 K, x(O)=0.0260, DTA
